(Bug #131, position 1: `The X is <call>.` declares X from what the call
 returns. A call with no arguments is written directly, and declares X the
 same way the call written with `of` does: a copy of the thing, not an
 address printed as a number.)

A thing called point has
  a number called x is 3,
  a number called y is 4.

To 'fresh point'.
  a point called made.
  Return a point, made.

To 'moved point' with a number called step.
  a point called made.
  Set made's x to step.
  Return a point, made.

The got is 'fresh point'.
Print got.
Print got's x add got's y.

The other is 'moved point' of 9.
Print other.

(Each call gives an independent copy.)
The second is 'fresh point'.
Set second's x to 30.
Print got.
Print second.
